# BOT DEE own-user context (always)

Resume: `@botdee-ctx$` / `$botdee-profile$`. Owner request Oct 29 2026: BOT DEE may use the signed-in patron's **own** username, height, location etc. — never the whole `users` table — with data classification and access rights enforced. Names stay as they are (BOT DEE brand, `floqAi` key, `floqai.html`); do not rename.

## Flow

```
My Privacy toggle (default OFF) → users/{uid}.botDeeProfileConsent = true (+ server-time stamp + version)
floqai.html → bot-dee-chat.js loadUserContext() → getBotDeeUserContext({})   (once per page session, memory only)
   server: auth → assertFeatureAccess(floqAi) → throttle 30/10 min → users/{request.auth.uid} only
           → botDeeFieldPolicy(dataClassification/botDeeUserContext) → buildUserContext → audit (names only)
own-profile question ("how tall am I") → answered locally from that context (client) / ownProfileAnswer (server)
anything else → executeBotSession → loadOwnUserContext(server) → promptBlock (redactSecrets) in Gemini system instruction
```

- **Never** a uid parameter, a collection query, `listDocuments`, or a directory lookup. `request.data` is ignored.
- The client never sends profile text to Gemini; the prompt block is assembled server-side from the same policy.
- Context lives in a JS variable keyed by uid; it is re-fetched after a uid change or page reload. Never `localStorage` / `sessionStorage` / IndexedDB.

## Tiers (`functions/data-classification-core.js` `BOT_DEE_FIELDS`, mirrored in `floqr-data-classification.js`)

| Tier | Fields | Returned when |
|---|---|---|
| No consent needed (non-PII) | `preferredLanguage`, `uiLanguage` + `audience` (viewer role) | always |
| Consent (internal) | `username`, `floqrHandle`, `displayName`, `firstName`, `height`, `heightUnit`, `city`, `country`, `musicInterests` | `botDeeProfileConsent === true` **and** Master Admin switch on |
| Never (restricted / secret) | `lastName`, `fullName`, `email`, `phone`, `birthMonth`, `birthDay`, `gender`, `taxiPickupAddress`, `stripeConnectAccountId` | never — `botDeeEligible = 0`, switch disabled, server refuses |
| Unknown | any other `users` field | never (builder walks the policy, not the doc) |

- Eligible = level in `public` / `internal` **and** name not matching `BOT_DEE_NEVER` (email, phone, birth, address, geo, token, stripe, payment, gender, …). A forged policy row cannot open a restricted field.
- Values are scrubbed (`sanitizeValue`): email-like, coordinates, ≥ 7 digits, street numbers in city/country are dropped; lists capped.
- Master Admin → Data Classification → **BOT DEE profile context** card toggles eligible fields → `setBotDeeFieldAccess` (SOS2FA + `FLOQRReasonPrompt` ≥ 8 + chained audit `dataClass.botDeeFieldsChanged`, "Nothing changed" guard). Saved in `dataClassification/botDeeUserContext {fields: {name: 0|1}, revision}`.

## Consent

- Field `users/{uid}.botDeeProfileConsent` (bool, strict `=== true`), `botDeeProfileConsentUpdatedAt` (`request.time`), `botDeeProfileConsentVersion` (`bdc-2026-10`). Rules: self only, boolean shape, server-time stamp, non-empty version ≤ 32. A `privacyConsents` row is appended for history.
- Withdraw = untick; the next fetch returns only the non-PII tier. Off-state reply points to My Profile → My Privacy (`floqai.chatProfileConsentOff`).

## Audit / throttle / logs

- Every `getBotDeeUserContext` call → unchained `featureServiceAuditLogs` row `botDee.user_context` (uid, role, `fieldNames`, `fieldCount`, consent, version, time). **Never values.**
- `executeBotSession` logs `userContext: auditDetail(...)` (names only). Throttle `botDeeContextThrottle/{uid}` 30 / 10 min (secret, Functions-only) → `resource-exhausted`, no read, no audit row.

